      "caption": "Heaven in one single pan 🤤  Ingredients:  • 4-6 chicken tenderloins • 2 tbsp olive oil • 1 tsp paprika • 1 tsp Italian seasoning • ¼ tsp salt • ¼ tsp black pepper • 4 cloves garlic, minced • 3/4 jar of sun dried tomatoes (in oil) • 1 cup orzo, uncooked • 2 cups chicken stock • 1/2 bag fresh spinach • ½ cup heavy cream • 1 tbsp dried basil • ¼ tsp red pepper flakes (more if you like it spicy) • parmesan for garnish Recipe: \t1.\tHeat up 2 tbsp of olive oil in a skillet over medium-high heat. \t2.\tSeason the sh*t out of that chicken with paprika, Italian seasoning, salt, and pepper \t3.\tSear for 3 minutes per side until golden and gorgeous, then yeet it out of the pan. \t4.\tAdd another splash of olive oil, garlic, chopped sun-dried tomatoes, and orzo.  \t5.\tToast the orzo for 2 minutes  \t6.\tPour in chicken stock + a sprinkle of salt, bring it to a boil, then cover so she can simmer down. \t7.\tCook for 5–8 minutes until the orzo is tender. Stir occasionally so it doesn’t stick like your ex. \t8.\tToss in spinach, cook till wilted (about 2–3 minutes, same amount of time it takes me to spiral). \t9.\tAdd heavy cream, dried basil, and red pepper flakes. Mix. \t10.\tAdd chicken back into the pan, let it simmer 2–5 minutes. \t11.\tFinish with parmesan on top!  #easydinner #dinnerideas #yummydinner #easyrecipes #madeandtaylored ",
